// Cast kit — the shapes the cast is built from.
//
// `Prop(beat)` is a scannable object: an Antivirus or a host scans a
// program's pass at it and the program is routed to one beat.
// `Person` marks a character who is a real body at the party — listed
// in the app's directory, messageable, able to share their codex.
// `Host` is a party host (faction Hosts); `Enforcer` is an Antivirus
// (faction Antivirus). Every door scan, every capture and every staff
// cue an Antivirus gets lives here, once, on the trait.
//
// Staff cues are `reply` lines: inside a character's own hook `self` is
// the character, so `reply` is a readout in THAT performer's booth (never
// a message to the guest). A broadcast `to group(Antivirus)` reaches no
// booth — performers are not members of anything — so it is never used.
//
// `playable: false` keeps a prop off the sign-in pickers: nobody *is*
// the Router.

TRAIT Prop(beat)
  playable: false
  when scanned by program:
    -> self.beat

TRAIT Person
  listed: true

TRAIT Host is Person
  faction: Hosts

  // A host scan never moves anyone. During the summons it is a check-in
  // at the Desktop; otherwise each host greets in their own voice
  // (every host owns `beat Greet(program)`, cast/hosts.loom).
  when scanned by program:
    if Night.summons_open == true and program.cleared:
      fire checked_in for program with at: The Desktop
      Self: You made it. Checked in.
    else:
      -> self.Greet

  // A host may clear a program's name.
  when vouch for program:
    set program.doubt = 0
    Self: {program.name} is a perfectly good program. I vouch for them. Move along.
    reply 🤝 Vouched for {program.name}. Their watchlist entry is cleared.

TRAIT Enforcer is Person
  faction: Antivirus

  // ── The door ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Every Antivirus scans with this one hook. Until an Antivirus clears
  // them, an uploaded program waits in the Mud Room, on rails.
  when scanned by program:
    if not program.uploaded:
      Self: Not yet. Finish your upload. I will be right here.
    else if not program.cleared:
      -> self.Clearance
    else if Night.summons_open == true:
      fire checked_in for program with at: The Desktop
      Self: Checked in. {program.name} is present at the Desktop.
    else:
      Self:
        cycle Scanning. Scanning. | {program.name}: no threats found. Today. | Your definitions are out of date. So are mine.

  // The inspection: free of viruses, through the Tube of lights, onto
  // the Desktop, and into Clippy's hands. Every line is a `Self:` line
  // (private to the program); the one `reply` is this performer's booth.
  beat Clearance(program)
    set program.cleared = true
    Self: Scanned. {program.name} is free of viruses and ready to explore the entire computer. There will be a game soon in the Desktop. Alexa will let you know when it's time to go there. Go through the Tube.
    Self: The Tube is a tunnel of lights. Wires. Chips. The cables brush your face like hair. Keep walking.
    move program to The Desktop
    reveal The Cache for program
    reveal Disk Cleanup for program
    reveal The Cloud for program
    reveal The Registry for program
    cue lights_tube_chase
    set Night.lights = "tube_chase"
    if Night.ads_started != true and Night.step < 4:
      set Night.ads_started = true
      cue terminals_attract
      set Night.terminals = "attract"
    Self: The Tube opens onto the Desktop: a blacked-out mess of LEDs, loose wire, encyclopaedias, computer parts and screens. A classic screensaver drifts across the TV above the fireplace. Everyone here is a program. Explore. Meet them.
    reply ✅ Cleared {program.name}.
    -> Orientation

  // ── To the Internet ───────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Never phase-guarded: it must capture any program at any time (the
  // reinstallation games' tests fire it on a fresh, un-uploaded persona).
  // During the Bingo results every capture gets the Bingo line and no
  // extra doubt; only the first fires Clippy's Corrupted Code speech,
  // unbound so it plays to the whole Desktop.
  when send to the internet for program:
    if program.corrupted == true:
      reply {program.name} is already in the Internet.
    else if Night.phase == "bingo_results":
      Self: {program.name}, you did not agree to be ruled by AI. That is what computer programs are here for. You have a virus that was not caught at the door. You are going to the Internet for a reinstallation.
      capture program into The Internet
      reply Logged: {program.name} sent to the Internet (Bingo).
      if Night.first_reinstall_done != true:
        set Night.first_reinstall_done = true
        set Night.first_reinstall = program.name
        fire first_reinstallation
    else:
      set program.doubt += 20
      Self: {program.name}. Corruption detected. You are going to the Internet for reinstallation. Do not resist the Tube.
      capture program into The Internet
      reply Logged: {program.name} sent to the Internet.

  // Never phase-guarded either.
  when mark as reinstalled for program:
    if program.corrupted:
      Self: {program.name} has demonstrated compliance. Reinstallation successful.
      release program from The Internet

  when accuse for program:
    set program.doubt += 25
    Self: I am watching you, {program.name}. Your behaviour has been logged.
    reply 👁 {program.name} is on the watchlist.

  // ── Booth cues (readouts for every Antivirus) ─────────────────────
  when call_to_the_desktop:
    if Night.step < 1:
      reply 🛡 Patrol the whole computer. Send every program to the Desktop.

  when hunt_time_up:
    if Night.phase == "hunt_1":
      reply 🛡 Sweep everyone back to the Desktop.

  when five_minute_warning:
    if Night.step < 9 and Night.summons_open != true and Night.summons_closed != true:
      reply 🛡 Scan every program arriving at the Desktop: that is their check-in.

  when zip_everyone_out:
    reply 🗜 Bring everyone out of the tent and zip them up.

  when advice_thwarted:
    if Night.phase == "advice" and Night.ended != true and Night.ending != "banished":
      reply ⛈ You are banished too. Go to the tent. Then turn on him: everyone does the hand jive, together.

  when go to the bathroom for program:
    reply 🚻 {program.name} is in Bathroom Mode. Not hacking the Internet.

  when program_late for program:
    reply ⏰ {program.name} is late for the Second Moment of Truth. Go get them.

  when sweep_requested:
    reply 🛡 Trabolta requests a sweep of {Night.sweep_target}.

  when alarm_tripped:
    reply 🚨 Server room breach. Get there. Anyone inside who is not a member of the winning faction goes to the Internet.
